Z||000002||theogre||10-29-2001||07:06 PM||||Those are the injector fuses for a V6. They aren't used on the TBI engines. tho this is an 84 and everything in 84 is wired wierd.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-29-2001||07:46 PM||||Why would an 84 Fiero that never had a V6 in the plan have a spot for fuses in the fuse box that would be required for a V6??||||reg||5
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||10-30-2001||07:06 PM||||Perhaps for the same reason the engine bay that never had a V8 in the plan, seems to have just enough room for one...<P>or maybe not...<P>Pontiac knew that they were going to have a GT coming up so they probably saved some money just using the same fuse box.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Rodrv6||10-30-2001||08:30 PM||||That fuse block is generic to a number of different GM models.  Saves production costs.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
